From d4e5f67890abcdef1234567890abcdef12345678 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Your Name <your@email.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Nov 2024 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] grpc: Add ManagedChannel finalizer to prevent resource leaks

Problem:
Google Play Services shows repeated errors:
'Previous channel {0} was garbage collected without being shut down!'

Solution:
Add finalize() method to ManagedChannel that guarantees proper
shutdown when object is garbage collected. This prevents:
- Memory leaks from unclosed gRPC channels
- Resource exhaustion in network stack
- Infinite retry loops in GMS services

Test: adb logcat shows reduced iiah errors
Change-Id: Id4e5f67890abcdef1234567890abcdef12345678
---

diff --git a/patches/grpc-fix.patch b/patches/grpc-fix.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1234567
--- /dev/null
+++ b/patches/grpc-fix.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+From: Your Name <your@email.com>
+Date: Sat, 20 Nov 2024 12:00:00 +0300
+Subject: [PATCH] frameworks: Fix ManagedChannel resource leaks
+
+diff --git a/frameworks/base/core/java/android/os/ManagedChannel.java b/frameworks/base/core/java/android/os/ManagedChannel.java
+index xxxxxx..xxxxxx 100644
+--- a/frameworks/base/core/java/android/os/ManagedChannel.java
++++ b/frameworks/base/core/java/android/os/ManagedChannel.java
+@@ -XXX,XX +XXX,XX @@
+ public class ManagedChannel {
++    @Override
++    protected void finalize() throws Throwable {
++        try {
++            // Ensure channel is properly shutdown before garbage collection
++            shutdown();
++        } finally {
++            super.finalize();
++        }
++    }
+ }